# PLAN3 DOCS — honest ooda bench

File: openOODA/audit/plan3_docs.oot
Wave 0. Ship 3. Survey only. Do not implement. Do not edit the public site.

Logline: Today ooda bench prints a false ok line. The target prints check FILE Nms from now_ms under TimeCap.

Setup: Worktree cli/cmd_more.oo and cli/main.oo. Plan: audit/plan_cli_bench.oot. C emit plus gcc remains product.

Beats:
  1. Record the false success line on disk.
  2. Name the honest print line and the TimeCap timer.
  3. Name no-args, missing file, and check-fail cases that must not print ok.
  4. Name optional --run after a passing check.
  5. Name help, Academy, and docs that stay unchanged.

## 1. Status

  Command `ooda bench` is residual. The stub is a lie.
  Status word: residual. This ship is open.

  TimeCap is a capability token. The runtime grants wall-clock
  access only when main takes `&TimeCap`. now_ms is the builtin
  that reads that token and returns integer milliseconds.

## 2. Today (false)

  File: cli/cmd_more.oo function run_ooda_bench.
  Signature: run_ooda_bench(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, args: List[String]).
  No TimeCap. No now_ms. No compiler check. No run.

  Both branches print the same line:
    ooda bench: ok
  Then the function returns. Exit is 0.

  cli/main.oo calls run_ooda_bench with the full argv. args[0]
  is the word bench. list_len(args) >= 1 is always true.
  The function then tests path_exists(fs, "."). That is the
  current directory. It is not the user file.
  If "." is missing, the last line still prints ooda bench: ok.

  So these all print ooda bench: ok and exit 0:
    ooda bench
    ooda bench --run
    ooda bench missing.oo
    ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo

  The file path is never read. Typecheck does not run.
  Wall time is not measured. --run does not run the file.

  Academy header in cmd_more.oo is also false for this ship:
    Logline says bench prints a success line.
    Setup says the command is not residual exit 2.

## 3. Help today (false)

  cli/main.oo print_help has one leftover line:
    ooda emit-health | errdigest | bench
  It does not name a file. It does not name --run.
  It groups bench with other stub floors.

  AGENTS.oot product-command list does not name bench.
  COOKBOOK.oot does not name bench.
  README.oot does not name product ooda bench.
  SHIPPED.oot and ROADMAP.oot do not name this command.
  scripts/benchmark.oo is a char-at loop. It is not ooda bench.

## 4. Target print line

  After a real check of FILE, print exactly one check line:
    ooda bench: check FILE Nms
  Example from the plan:
    ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 12ms

  Grammar:
    1. Prefix: ooda bench: check
    2. One space. Then FILE as the user path.
    3. One space. Then N as a decimal integer. N >= 0.
    4. Then the letters ms with no space.

  N is wall time of the check phase. Take t0 = now_ms(time)
  before the check. Take t1 = now_ms(time) after the check.
  N is t1 - t0. If t1 < t0, print 0ms. Do not print a date.
  Do not call date. Do not use a SysCap shell timer.

  The line measures the compiler check. It is not a microbench
  of user code. Do not claim loop-body speed unless --run runs.

  Do not print ooda bench: ok after this ship.

## 5. TimeCap

  DE2 adds time: &TimeCap to cli/main.oo main.
  DE2 passes that token into run_ooda_bench.
  Name the parameter time. C emit already grants
    long long time = oo_cap_grant_time();
  in every main. RT must prove the seed compiler accepts
    main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String]).
  If that signature fails typecheck, COORD stops ship 3.
  Do not fall back to date. Do not patch oodac or chs_rt.

## 6. No-args and missing file

  These must not print ooda bench: ok. They must not print
  a check FILE Nms line. Exit must not be 0.

  No file (ooda bench, or only flags):
    Print: ooda bench: missing file
    Exit 2.
    Same words as ooda check and ooda test.

  FILE is absent on disk:
    Print: ERR<TAB>bench<TAB>unreadable file: FILE
    Exit 2.
    Same form as ooda check.

  ooda bench --run with no file is the no-file case.
  Do not treat --run as a path.

  args[0] is bench. The file is the first later token that
  does not start with -.

## 7. Check fail

  Run the real compiler check. Same find_oodac path as
  ooda check. Do not invent a second compiler.

  If check fails:
    Exit non-zero.
    Print that check failed.
    Do not print a run line.
    Do not print a fake time for a run that did not start.
    If the check did run, check-phase Nms may print.
    Never print ooda bench: ok.

## 8. Optional --run

  Flag: --run. After a passing check only.

  Second line:
    ooda bench: run FILE Nms
  Same grammar as the check line. N is now_ms delta for
  the run phase. Two now_ms calls. No list growth.

  If check fails, skip --run. No run line.
  Hang budget on fixtures/hello.oo: 30 seconds when --run
  emits and links.

  Use the product run helper path. Do not exec the user
  file with sh -c. Do not exec the bench target through a
  new shell. SysCap may start oodac the same way ooda check
  and ooda run already do.

## 9. Constraint for DE1

  host_run.oo is shared read-only.
  run_oodac and run_oodac_check call process_exit.
  If bench calls those helpers, it cannot print Nms after
  the child ends. DE1 must start the same oodac check (and
  optional run) so the Result comes back, then print, then
  exit with that status. Do not edit host_run.oo.
  Import find_compiler.oo if needed. It is read-only.

## 10. Help target

  Only this ship edits cli/main.oo.
  main.oo is 254 lines. Limit is 256.
  Replace the leftover group line. Keep other dispatch.

  Required help text:
    ooda bench <file.oo> [--run]

  One extra println fits. If help cannot fit, DE2 splits
  print_help into cli_help.oo. COORD records the split.

  After the change, ooda help must name the real command.
  It must not list bench as a bare floor next to emit-health.

## 11. Academy on product files

  After Wave 1, cmd_more.oo Logline must not say bench
  prints a success line. Other stubs (em, migrate, install,
  context-pack, emit-health, errdigest) stay. They are not
  this ship. pack still writes the air-gap tree.

  New scripts/bench_smoke.oo needs a 4-element Academy
  header. Strictly <= 256 lines. No .md .py extra .sh.

