  Known external lock (out of ship 3 write set):
    openOODA/qa/e2e_spine.oo wants
    ./bin/ooda bench to print ooda bench: ok.
  Do not keep the stub to satisfy that script.
  QA owns that file later.

## 13. Honest claim

  ooda bench FILE times a real typecheck of FILE.
  Default is check wall ms only.
  --run adds a second timed product run after check pass.
  That is still program start through the product run path.
  It is not a loop microbench of user code.
  scripts/benchmark.oo remains a different tool.

## 14. Done when (docs view)

  1. ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo prints
     ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo Nms with N >= 0.
  2. ooda bench with no file does not print ooda bench: ok.
  3. Missing file does not print ooda bench: ok. Exit 2.
  4. strings on bin/ooda has no ooda bench: ok.
  5. Help names ooda bench <file.oo> [--run].
  6. Optional --run after check pass prints a run Nms line.
  7. Public site is unchanged.

C emit plus gcc remains the product path.
